    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) stand out as our most efficient starts. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta; specifically, Peralta\u2019s slow delivery provides a boost to our aggressive base-running strategy, which is critical given our focus on the scarcity of stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** faces a high-xERA opponent in Bradford, and the combination of park factors and the pitcher\u2019s skill profile creates a clear path to high-level production. We are also looking at **Jackson Merrill** (69.57) as a strong play; his matchup against Bibee is mitigated by a high dynamic platoon edge, solidifying his spot as a daily anchor.\n\nOur most difficult decision occurred at the bottom of the order, where **Coby Mayo** (43.08) narrowly missed the cut. While **Coby Mayo** profiles well against Peralta, his low batting order placement and the slight park disadvantage pushed his efficiency score just below our target threshold, resulting in him staying on the bench. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Kyle Tucker** (51.47); his base projection remains elite, but a difficult matchup against Henderson\u2014a pitcher with a 2.84 xERA\u2014drags his efficiency down significantly today, though he remains in the utility slot due to his inherent upside. We are continuing to monitor the roster for any late-breaking weather or lineup changes, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order, as their high-volume plate appearances are vital to our daily offensive floor. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving our bench depth limited as we navigate this stretch of the season.",
